# This repo is authored on Windows and DEPLOYED on Linux. Anything the Linux box
# executes or parses must arrive with LF endings, or it fails in ways that read
# as anything but a line ending:
#
#   - a systemd unit with CRLF takes the \r as part of the value
#   - a script with `#!/usr/bin/env python3\r` reports "no such file or
#     directory" naming an interpreter that plainly exists
#
# The creature's hands are the sharp case: a broken shebang there would make
# every tool call fail while the tool itself was perfectly good -- the framework
# breaking the work and the creature being billed for it, which this project has
# already paid for three times.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
hands/* text eol=lf
